@startuml
title How an action command is assembled before reaching the shell
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam ArrowColor #B54A4A
skinparam activity {
  BackgroundColor #FDEEEE
  BorderColor #B54A4A
  DiamondBackgroundColor #FFFFFF
  DiamondBorderColor #B54A4A
}

start
:actionban template from the action file\ne.g. "<iptables> -I f2b-<name> 1 -s <ip> -j <blocktype>";
:replaceTag: static properties from [Init]\nrecursive, cached, family-conditional;
note right
  Bounded by MAX_TAG_REPLACE_COUNT
  to stop self-referencing definitions
end note
:replaceDynamicTags: ticket values\n<ip>, <failures>, <matches>, <F-USER>;
if (value contains a shell metacharacter?) then (yes)
  :bind it to a shell variable f2bV_<tag>\nand pass it as a positional argument;<<#EEF5FF>>
else (no)
  :inline the value in the command text;
endif
:buildShellCmd produces\n["f2bV_x=$0 \n <command>", value];
:Utils.executeCmd runs it with shell=True\nin a new session, timeout 60 s;
if (exit code 0?) then (no)
  :run actioncheck, then actionrepair\nand retry once;<<#FFF6F6>>
endif
stop
@enduml
